The tunnel engine is wireguard-go (MIT), used as a Go module.
It is not vendored line-by-line in this repository.
Windows loads the official Wintun prebuilt DLL beside the executable.
That DLL is covered by the Wintun prebuilt-binary license, which permits
redistribution alongside an application that uses the Wintun API.
The DLL is downloaded by scripts/fetch-wintun.sh and is not modified.

macOS NetworkExtension source links WireGuardKit from wireguard-apple (MIT).
That project is not copied into git. macos/build-macos.sh pins tag 1.0.16-27.

No GPL-licensed source is copied here.

Optional v2fly geoip.dat is CC-BY-SA-4.0:
https://github.com/v2fly/geoip/releases/tag/202611080027
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
The file is downloaded by scripts/fetch-geo-dat.mjs and is not stored in git.
Country prefix exclusions are off unless geo routing is turned on. Off keeps
the full 0.0.0.0/0 and ::/0 capture, the fail-closed kill switch, and DNS
inside the tunnel.
Tor is not bundled. The client speaks to a Tor the user installs.
